    'akademik-almir-badnjevic-izabran-za-predsjednika-iasabih-a',
    'Akademik Almir Badnjević izabran za predsjednika Internacionalne akademije nauka i umjetnosti u Bosni i Hercegovini',
    'Academician Almir Badnjević elected President of the International Academy of Sciences and Arts in Bosnia and Herzegovina',
    'Aktuelnosti',
    'News',
    'Akademik prof. dr. Almir Badnjević izabran je za novog predsjednika IASABIH-a na vanrednoj elektronskoj sjednici Skupštine Akademije održanoj 6. novembra 2026. godine.',
    'Academician Prof. Dr. Almir Badnjević was elected the new President of IANUBIH at an extraordinary electronic session of the Academy’s General Assembly held on 6 November 2026.',
    'Sarajevo, 7. novembar 2026. godine – Akademik prof. dr. Almir Badnjević izabran je za novog predsjednika Internacionalne akademije nauka i umjetnosti u Bosni i Hercegovini (IASABIH), nakon smrti njenog osnivača i dugogodišnjeg predsjednika, akademika prof. dr. Asima Kurjaka.

Izbor je potvrđen na vanrednoj elektronskoj sjednici Skupštine Akademije, održanoj 6. novembra 2026. godine, u skladu s utvrđenim protokolom. Akademik Badnjević jedan je od osnivača Akademije, a u njenom početnom periodu obavljao je i dužnost izvršnog direktora, učestvujući zajedno s akademikom Kurjakom u uspostavljanju organizacijskih i institucionalnih temelja njenog rada.

Preuzimajući dužnost, Badnjević je zahvalio članovima Skupštine na povjerenju, kao i dosadašnjem rukovodstvu i saradnicima koji su doprinijeli razvoju Akademije. Posebno je istakao odgovornost očuvanja naučnog i institucionalnog naslijeđa akademika Asima Kurjaka. „Asim je vjerovao u ovu Akademiju. Zajedno smo je stvarali. Danas, uz povjerenje kolegica i kolega, preuzimam odgovornost da ono što smo započeli ne ostane samo uspomena na njega, nego djelo koje će trajati, a koliko smo u tome uspjeli, neće pokazati naše riječi, nego ono što ostane iza nas“, poručio je Badnjević.

Akademik Almir Badnjević (40) univerzitetski je profesor na Univerzitetu u Sarajevu, s međunarodnim akademskim angažmanima na univerzitetima u Warwicku (UK), Rimu (Italija) i Podgorici (Crna Gora). Doktorirao je 2015. godine na Fakultetu elektrotehnike i računarstva Univerziteta u Zagrebu. Njegov naučni rad obuhvata biomedicinski inženjering, medicinske uređaje, metrologiju i primjenu vještačke inteligencije. Učestvovao je u razvoju sistema inspekcije medicinskih uređaja i uspostavljanju laboratorijske infrastrukture u više od 20 zemalja svijeta. Autor je i koautor više od 200 naučnih i stručnih publikacija, s h-indeksom 41 i 5.977 citata, prema podacima iz novembra 2026. godine. Spada među 2% najcitiranijih naučnika u svijetu. Fellow je Svjetske akademije umjetnosti i nauka (WAAS), redovni član Evropske akademije nauka i umjetnosti (EASA), Fellow međunarodnih organizacija IUPESM i AAIA, te UN Cyber Fellow. Aktivno djeluje u stručnim tijelima IEEE-a i komisiji za digitalne tehnologije i vještačku inteligenciju Evropskih olimpijskih komiteta. Trenutno obavlja dužnost direktora Agencije za identifikacione dokumente, evidenciju i razmjenu podataka Bosne i Hercegovine (IDDEEA).

U narednom periodu Akademija će poseban naglasak staviti na jačanje međunarodne naučne i umjetničke saradnje, istraživačke projekte, kvalitet naučnih publikacija, podršku mladim istraživačima i veću vidljivost rezultata svojih članova. Istovremeno s izborom novog predsjednika, u rad je puštena i nova internetska stranica Akademije, dostupna na adresi https://www.iasabih.ba, koja će služiti predstavljanju aktivnosti, članstva, naučnih i umjetničkih dostignuća te budućih projekata Akademije.

Izbor novog predsjednika dolazi u danima oproštaja od akademika Asima Kurjaka. Nakon komemoracije održane 2. novembra u Narodnom pozorištu Sarajevo, za 9. novembar najavljena je i komemoracija u zagrebačkom Muzeju Mimara.

Internacionalna akademija nauka i umjetnosti u Bosni i Hercegovini nastavlja svoj rad s opredjeljenjem da čuva naslijeđe svog osnivača i razvija se kao mjesto međunarodnog povezivanja, naučne izvrsnosti, umjetničkog stvaralaštva i slobodne akademske misli.',
    'Sarajevo, 7 November 2026 – Academician Prof. Dr. Almir Badnjević has been elected the new President of the International Academy of Sciences and Arts in Bosnia and Herzegovina (IANUBIH), following the death of its founder and long-serving President, Academician Prof. Dr. Asim Kurjak.

The election was confirmed at an extraordinary electronic session of the Academy’s General Assembly held on 6 November 2026, in accordance with the established protocol. Academician Badnjević is one of the Academy’s founders and served as its Executive Director during its formative period, working alongside Academician Kurjak to establish the organisational and institutional foundations of its work.

Upon assuming office, Badnjević thanked the members of the General Assembly for their confidence, as well as the previous leadership and associates who contributed to the Academy’s development. He particularly emphasised the responsibility of preserving the scientific and institutional legacy of Academician Asim Kurjak. “Asim believed in this Academy. We built it together. Today, with the confidence of my colleagues, I assume the responsibility of ensuring that what we began does not remain merely a memory of him, but becomes a lasting achievement. The measure of our success will not be our words, but what remains after us,” Badnjević said.

Academician Almir Badnjević (40) is a university professor at the University of Sarajevo, with international academic engagements at universities in Warwick (United Kingdom), Rome (Italy) and Podgorica (Montenegro). He received his doctorate in 2015 from the Faculty of Electrical Engineering and Computing at the University of Zagreb. His scientific work encompasses biomedical engineering, medical devices, metrology and the application of artificial intelligence. He has participated in the development of medical-device inspection systems and the establishment of laboratory infrastructure in more than 20 countries. He is the author or co-author of more than 200 scientific and professional publications, with an h-index of 41 and 5,977 citations as of November 2026. He ranks among the world’s top 2% most-cited scientists. He is a Fellow of the World Academy of Art and Science (WAAS), a full member of the European Academy of Sciences and Arts (EASA), a Fellow of the international organisations IUPESM and AAIA, and a UN Cyber Fellow. He is active in IEEE professional bodies and in the European Olympic Committees’ commission for digital technology and artificial intelligence. He currently serves as Director of the Agency for Identification Documents, Registers and Data Exchange of Bosnia and Herzegovina (IDDEEA).

In the coming period, the Academy will place particular emphasis on strengthening international scientific and artistic cooperation, research projects, the quality of scientific publications, support for young researchers and greater visibility of its members’ achievements. Alongside the election of the new President, the Academy’s new website has also been launched at https://www.iasabih.ba. It will present the Academy’s activities, membership, scientific and artistic achievements, and future projects.

The election of the new President comes during a period of mourning for Academician Asim Kurjak. Following the commemoration held on 2 November at the National Theatre Sarajevo, another commemoration has been announced for 9 November at the Mimara Museum in Zagreb.

The International Academy of Sciences and Arts in Bosnia and Herzegovina continues its work with a commitment to preserving the legacy of its founder and developing as a place of international connection, scientific excellence, artistic creation and free academic thought.',
